B.a3B=new A.c4(B.a4z,["Intro","Database","Tracking","Settings","Appearance","Dark (default) or light preset \u2014 applies to the whole app immediately.","Dark","Light","Language","Introduction","Unlock learning & app features","Placement, unlock quiz, deep-dive topics, infographic, and learning quizzes (stages 1\u20133) \u2014 work through them in order.","SOL \u2014 Soldier of Light","Not another calorie counter. SOL is active control: plan, execute, optimize.","Stylized scene: the path forward and staying consistent\u2014whether you\u2019re new or a long way in.","The concept","SOL doesn't force you into rigid plans \u2014 it gives you a system.\nYou set your goals; SOL distributes macros intelligently across your meals and suggests the right combination.","Aggressive Cut & Lean Bulk","Aggressive Cut: a very strict diet phase \u2014 a clear calorie deficit and tight adherence, so you lose fat while doing your best to keep muscle.\n\nLean Bulk: clean, controlled muscle building \u2014 a modest surplus and focused macros so you grow without piling on unnecessary fat.","The four modes","Maintenance: hold your current mass, flexible everyday eating.\nAggressive Cut: clear deficit while protecting muscle.\nLean Bulk: clean surplus for growth without fat gain.\nAdvanced: manual control or preset slider (Aggressive Cut \u2194 Dirty Bulk).","Why macros \u2014 not calories","First, the frame: food is meant to fuel you. What you eat beyond your needs for a long time, your body happily stores as fat \u2014 a reserve.\n\nCalories only tell you how much you ate. Macros tell you what your body does with it. That's why SOL asks only for macros \u2014 calories are derived.\n\nA calorie deficit alone doesn't mean fat loss: without enough protein, your body burns muscle. With enough protein and the right distribution, you protect muscle and target fat specifically.","How your body works",'Fat is an energy store. Surplus calories get stored \u2014 no matter if from fat, carbs or protein. A deficit draws from that store. What actually gets burned depends on your hormonal and nutrient profile. Building blocks: 1 g protein = 4 kcal, 1 g carbs = 4 kcal, 1 g fat = 9 kcal. In a deficit, your body may also tap muscle protein \u2014 so "eat less" without protein is not enough.\n\n\u2022 High protein (in SOL, up to 2.5 g/kg BW) \u2192 signal: "keep muscle".\n\u2022 Enough fat (0.75 g/kg BW) \u2192 hormones stay stable.\n\u2022 Carbs as the remainder \u2192 energy for training and brain.\n\nThat\'s why SOL\'s macro priority is: Protein \u2192 Fat \u2192 Carbs.',"Macro priority","1. Protein: protects muscle, keeps you full, high thermic effect.\n2. Fat: hormones, cell membranes, nutrient uptake, recovery.\n3. Carbs: energy for performance and brain \u2014 scaled to your target.","Recognizing macros in food (short)","Rough rules for eyeballing and shopping \u2014 exact numbers are in the database per 100 g.\n\n\u2022 Complex carbs: starch-heavy \u2014 e.g. potatoes, rice, oats, whole grains, pasta, legumes.\n\u2022 Simple carbs: sweet stuff and fast hits \u2014 sugar, fruit & fructose in juices, soda, many pastries; zero-cal sweeteners don\u2019t count as sugar here (almost no kcal).\n\u2022 Protein: rule of thumb \u2014 often foods that are solid/chunky: meat, fish, eggs, quark/cottage cheese, cheese, tofu (pure oil or pure sugar syrup isn\u2019t protein).\n\u2022 Fat: oily, buttery, creamy, nuts, seeds, avocado, dairy fat \u2014 lots of energy in a small volume.","How to use SOL","1. Settings: pick a mode, enter weight and body fat \u2014 SOL calculates your macros, calories are derived. Weekly charts/balances live in Settings too.\n2. Tracking: add foods per meal, or use the Generator for smart combinations.\n3. Daily: log weight, add notes, reset the day if needed.","Pre & Post Workout \u2014 Performance","Pre- and post-workout meals aren\u2019t ordinary meals \u2014 they\u2019re tuned for performance.\n\nPre-workout: you give your body the part of the day\u2019s energy it actually needs before training \u2014 fast-available carbs to top up glycogen, a bit of protein to protect muscle. You don\u2019t walk into the gym tired, you walk in loaded.\n\nPost-workout: right after training the tanks are empty \u2014 glycogen is used up, muscle fibres are stressed. That\u2019s exactly when your body absorbs nutrients most efficiently. Carbs refill the stores, protein kicks off repair. This is the window where training actually turns into growth.\n\nThat\u2019s why these two meals stay together as a block in SOL \u2014 they belong to the training and are planned together.","Mindset","Discipline beats motivation. Every meal is a decision. SOL gives you the structure \u2014 you bring the execution.","Nutrition at a glance","The same story as your Notion one-pager \u2014 as a clean SOL-style schematic (no cartoon asset), plus the colored cards below in your language.","Quick map: a functional mix (fuel, hormones, muscle) vs. quick excess (more body-fat storage). Details are in the tiles \u2014 same logic as your overview.","Structure & energy (schematic)","Carbs \xb7 fuel","Fat \xb7 hormones","Protein \xb7 muscle","Functional mix: everyday life, training, recovery",'Lots of sugary + hard-fat combos / chronic surplus \u2192 body fat as a "reserve tank" more than performance',"Healthy fats","The body needs them for hormones and restorative sleep, among other jobs.\n\nPart of the calories goes to messengers, cell structure, and repair \u2014 you usually need only a modest share. Examples: avocado, olive oil, nuts.\n\nOnly a little is needed \u2014 also for heart health, hormone balance, and sleep.","Healthy carbs = energy","Steady fuel for the day, brain, and training \u2014 e.g. potatoes, rice, oats, legumes, whole grain.\n\nSimple vs complex (worth spotting day to day): complex carbs (starch, often with fiber) usually release energy more slowly and keep you fuller longer. Simple carbs (sugar, sweet drinks, lots of white flour) hit faster and can pack many kcal without much volume \u2014 in SOL you can see sugar and \u201ccomplex\u201d lines in the database.","Protein","Builds and repairs tissue (including muscle) and helps satiety \u2014 e.g. salmon, beef, eggs, quark or cottage cheese.\n\nStrength training & muscle retention: often 1.4\u20132.5 g protein per kg body weight (e.g. 80 kg: about 112\u2013200 g per day). To keep or build muscle, plan toward the upper half of that band \u2014 SOL typically uses up to 2.5 g/kg as an explainable default ceiling.","Sugary carbs & unhealthy fats","Burgers, fries, donuts, bacon, a lot of deep-fried food: calories add up fast, often with little fiber and satiety.\n\nA common pattern: very sugary drinks and snacks together with lots of hard/saturated fat \u2014 that mix makes a chronic surplus easy.\n\nExcess energy from these combos tends to be stored as body fat.","What you don\u2019t need right now is often stashed as fat \u2014 \u201cstored energy\u201d for harder days (a reserve).","Common daily calorie split (rule of thumb)","50 %\nCarbs","30 %\nProtein","20 %\nFat","SOL derives your macros from weight, body fat, and goal \u2014 50/30/20 is not a fixed rule here.","Takeaways","Protein = repair \u2192 growth \u2192 strength","Healthy fats = important, but only in small amounts.","Complex carbs = energy \u2014 chronic excess tends to be stored as fat.","Learning stages (quiz)","Topics: SOL, macros & training (same thread as a Notion-style plan). Short, playful questions. Stage 2 unlocks after stage 1 is fully correct; stage 3 after 1 and 2 are done.","Stage {n}","Quiz","Stage {n}","Not quite\u2014try another answer.","Finish the previous stage fully first.","Stage {n} done\u2014nice work!","Full text unlocks after you pass the unlock quiz (max. 3 tries per day).","Unlock the write-ups","Read the first two topics, then take the short check (3 questions). That reveals the rest of the intro, the infographic, and the learning stages \u2014 later, each block can gate app features.","Open unlock quiz","Tries today: {n} / {m}","At most 3 tries per day. Try again tomorrow \u2014 or get them all right in one go.","Write-ups unlocked \u2014 good luck with SOL.","Introduction \u2014 unlock check","Which best describes SOL?","A flexible system: your goals map to macros per meal \u2014 not a rigid weekly menu.","A fixed 7-day plan you must never adjust or skip.","Only a calorie target; how you split P/C/F barely matters.","Typical macro priority in SOL (first concern)?","Protein first (muscle & satiety), then sensible fat, then mostly carbs for energy","As few calories as possible, whether from sugar or protein only.","Fat must be zero or you cannot make progress.","Why have a sensible fat minimum (rule of thumb per kg body weight)?","Only for taste, with no other role in the body.","For hormone- and cell-related building blocks \u2014 not optional filler.","Fat fully replaces every calorie from carbohydrates.","Placement \u2014 knowledge check","Exit","Finish the short placement quiz in Introduction first.","Placement required","Seven quick questions on nutrition & macros (including simple vs. complex carbs; aligned with your Notion-style overview). We set your starting tier (1\u20133). Then Database, Tracking, and Settings unlock.","Start placement","Starting tier {n} \xb7 {c}/{m} correct. Let\u2019s go!","Placement: tier {n}","Knowledge","{p} / {t} learning-check questions answered","Ready?","You can reread this anytime. To get started: set your mode, weight, and body fat in Settings \u2014 then log your meals in Tracking. Plan first, day-to-day second.","Open Settings","Open Tracking","Which role does protein play most of all in the body?","Mainly the brain\u2019s fastest fuel","Build and repair tissue (including muscle)","Hormone production only","What do healthy fats usually support in a modest, appropriate amount?","Hormone balance, cell structure; also sleep and recovery","So you can drop all carbs","The body does not need fat at all","In practice, what\u2019s the main difference between complex vs. (mostly) simple carbohydrates?","Complex carbs (starch, often with fiber) usually fill you longer and raise blood sugar more gently; simple ones act faster (sugar, many sodas, white flour pastries, \u2026).","There\u2019s no real difference \u2014 it\u2019s all marketing","Simple carbs are always the healthier choice","If you eat much more than you burn for a long time, the typical outcome is:","It all leaves the body unused","Energy is often stored as body fat, among other places","Only protein is stored that way","Common rough pie-chart splits (carb / protein / fat, % of kcal) look like","20 / 50 / 30","50 / 30 / 20","10 / 80 / 10","A lot of very sugary, fried, and ultra-processed food typically means that","You gain lean muscle with no training","Dense kcal add up fast and weight gain (often fat) gets more likely","Body fat cannot change","Why is protein at the front in SOL (and good practice), especially in a deficit?","It signals the body to keep lean mass in reach","Protein cannot be used for energy at all","Carbs do not matter and can be ignored","Daily overview","Combined meal","Combined meal","Day target (mid) {goal} kcal \xb7 eaten {eaten} kcal \xb7 left {rest} kcal","Choose meals","All meals","Selected meals","Split by meal","Performance note (pre-workout)","Pre-workout is performance-based \u2014 merging with other meals may affect training. Continue anyway?","Combined meal","Total: {eaten} / {target} kcal ({delta})","Still open: {rest} kcal","Eaten: {eaten} kcal","{v} open","Includes: {m}","Enable","Disable","In combined meal","This meal is bundled \u2014 track via the combined meal section above.","Go to combined meal","Add to which meal?","Open generator","Continue anyway","OK","Total food volume today (g)","Meal amount","Note: the soft daily kcal tip only nudges upward after 3+ logged days in a row. If your body isn\u2019t changing, follow the green daily band first.","Meal kcal display","Simple: target center + green band. Advanced: min/max numbers as now.","Simple","Advanced","Last meal (kcal)","For the last non-snack meal (usually dinner) the kcal band can follow what is left for the day \u2014 chosen once per day.","Ask before logging","When on: before the first add (food, generator, AI) for that meal, choose macro band vs. day remainder. Off = always use the macro band.","Last meal: how much?","How many kcal should the last meal of today get?","Normal share of this meal","Everything left for the day","Keep some for snacks","Target center: {k} kcal","Lower","Upper","One bar: your actual kcal. Two marks: lower and upper. ~10% extra width past the top mark for the red over zone. Target center is above. Green in band, gold below, red over.","Bar: logged kcal. Vertical line: lower bound. Green when within range.","Already in your database","This code matches a saved food \u2014 track it or create another entry (e.g. new batch).","Name already used","You already have a custom food with this name. Compare the values \u2014 you can cancel or add another entry anyway.","Saved item","Add anyway","Barcode already in your database","This barcode is already linked. Only one custom entry is allowed per barcode \u2014 you cannot save a second one with the same code.","OK","Add to tracking","Create from preview","Edit amount (g)","Big surplus? Name it to stay in control","Only conscious eating and clear decisions make lasting success. Eating more once in a while is fine\u2014what matters is keeping control, staying the one who decides, and not handing food the power over your mood. You can mark a cheat day to stay honest on the books\u2014or keep going if that fits you.","Cheat day & plan","Not now","Daily kcal over your target","So far: {eaten} kcal \xb7 goal: {goal} kcal \u2014 surplus +{over} kcal.","Rule of thumb: about {steps} extra walking steps \u2248 +{kcal} kcal for your weight (rough estimate; movement is not a perfect offset).","In \xabCut\xbb (Di\xe4t) mode, SOL can only credit up to +{cap} kcal from \xabExtra steps (today)\xbb \u2014 if your surplus is larger, that won\u2019t cover all of it in the app.","Apply extra steps (in SOL)","Log a cheat day & stay honest","Ignore: weaker control & focus","Then measurable progress is easier to sideline, your body is more likely to store excess as fat, and quick, often hyper\u2011palatable calories tend to nudge people away from clear choices. You still decide\u2014SOL keeps logging honestly.","Extra steps for today updated (+{k} kcal in the plan, within SOL\u2019s cap).","Raising plan steps like this is available in \xabCut\xbb (Di\xe4t) mode. The number above is a rough real-world ballpark only.","Approx. kcal \u201csaved\u201d this week (cut, where applicable): {k} kcal","Rough fat-mass equivalent (~7000 kcal \u2248 1 kg): \u2248 {f} kg","Lock screen widget: on Android/iOS, add a widget/shortcut in system settings; the app does not yet ship a built-in tile for that.","Day","Today","7-day stats (details)","Week \u0394 (kg)","Streak","Goal","Plan","Second workout per day","For athletes training twice a day (Advanced only). Shares are split \u2013 then adjust each meal's calories above.","One workout","Normal: pre- and post-workout","+ Pre-workout 2","Extra meal before the second session","+ Pre- & post-workout 2","Second session with a meal before and after","Switch to \u201cplanned\u201d","Not eaten yet \u2013 counts once you log it","Switched to planned","Move to another meal","Change amount","Adjust grams or portion","Remove from today's tracking","Recipes with {n}","No recipes or own meals with this food yet.","Enter values for","Portion / piece","e.g. 1 kebab","1 portion","Enter values for the whole portion \u2013 PREPIT converts to 100 g and saves the portion as an amount.","= per 100 g:","Set as default display","Default display in database","Meal times","Plan meal times","Show time + window on each meal, optionally as calendar reminders.","First meal at","Gap between meals","Auto ({h} h)","Time window","Your plan","Auto: 3 meals \u2192 every 4 h, 4 meals \u2192 every 3 h. Pre- to post-workout = 2 h (training). Tap to set a time yourself (*).","Automatic","Add reminders to calendar","Downloads a calendar file: daily repeating events with a notification at meal time. On iPhone tap \u201cAdd All\u201d. After changes, delete the old events and add again.","Calendar file created","Calendar file isn't available here","Time for {m} \u2013 log it in PREPIT.","Still free today","End combined meal","Where should the combined meal's entries go?","All into","Or one by one","Move & end","of which {g} g sugar","of which sugar (optional)","All carbs count for the units \u2013 not just sugar. Sugar only shows how fast it hits the blood.","Carbs & diabetes","What happens: carbs turn into sugar (glucose) in the body \u2013 blood sugar rises. Whether from bread, rice, fruit or sweets.\nSugar vs. carbs: sugar is only part of the carbs. For blood sugar all carbs count, not just sugar.\nSimple (fast): sugar, white flour, juice, sweets \u2013 enter the blood quickly.\nComplex (slow): whole grain, oats, legumes, potatoes \u2013 slower and steadier.\nBrakes: fibre, protein and fat in the same meal slow the rise.\nKE / BE: estimation units for carbs \u2013 1 KE = 10 g, 1 BE = 12 g. Many diabetics plan meals and insulin with them.\nIn PREPIT: enable diabetes mode in settings \u2013 you'll see units per food, meal and day plus the calculator.\nImportant: PREPIT does not calculate insulin doses. Always set doses and targets with your doctor / diabetes team.","Per 100 g \xb7 {k} kcal","{u} calculator","1 {u} = {g} g carbs","from {g} g carbs","Pick a food or enter carbs","Food","Enter carbs","Amount","Guidance only \u2013 always dose insulin per your doctor's plan.","Food + amount","Search food \u2026","Carbs directly","Carbohydrates","Missing product? Look it up online or ask an AI, then add it here.","Quick add","Amount","Portions (optional)","Add portion","e.g. 1 pizza","Type (diet / bulk)","Brand / variant (optional)","e.g. Dr. Oetker","Photo","Classification","All","Today","Week/Month","Week/Month","fast carbs","fast carbs \u2014 good around training","eaten often","high volume","compact","slow carbs","Show all ({n})","Show less","fast","slow","Carbs today: {v} {u}","Diabetes","I have diabetes","Shows carb units everywhere, marks fast \u26a1 and slow \ud83d\udc22 carbs, and the generator prefers slow carbs. Cut, bulk & everyday modes keep working.","Carb unit","CU (10 g carbs)","BU (12 g carbs)","Important: PREPIT does not calculate insulin doses. Carb units are estimates from the database \u2014 always dose according to your doctor's plan or your diabetes app/pump.","Still open","Exact fit: {g} g","Use","Tap = add/remove \xb7 Long-press = main aisle (gold)","Delete tag \u201c{t}\u201d?","e.g. 2 packs, 500 g","Aisle","Tags","New tag, e.g. Aldi \u2026","One list","By aisle","What do you need?","All","All done \u2014 nothing left on the list.","To buy","Recently bought","Tap = bought \xb7 Long-press = amount, aisle, tags (e.g. Aldi) \xb7 Filter by tags above.","Choose your own food \u2026","Amount (optional)","Empty = calculate automatically","Automatic","Recipes","For","Goal","Taste","Food","Search, scan, recent","Meal","Template, amounts fitted","Combos matching your macros","AI photo","Snap a photo, estimate values","Undo","Last meal: rest of the day","Last meal: normal share","Change","Reset","Swap","Swap {n}","Most similar macros first \u2014 amounts are recalculated.","Meals","Add \u201c{n}\u201d to \u2026","Quick add","E.g. eating out: enter a name and rough macros (quick search) \u2014 no weighing. Counts once for today.","Name (e.g. Grandma's noodles)","Meal","Also save to database","Add","1 portion = 100 g","{n} added: {k} kcal \xb7 {m}","Add meal","Generator","Combined","Individual","via daily overview","This meal","Rest of day","Vegan","\ud83c\udf31 Vegan","Generator: rest of day","\ud83d\udd58 Recent","last {g} g","All foods today","Eaten today \u2014 total","Sort:","Amount","Now: {g} g \xb7 {k} kcal","New total amount","Split proportionally across all meals it's logged in.","Delete all","Generator","Advanced","Open","Cut \xb7 volume","Normal","Bulk \xb7 compact","Any","Ready combos","Build your own","OPTION","RECIPE","Add","Protein source","Carb source","Fat source (optional)","missing","No matching foods \u2014 try another flavor or goal.","This meal is already full.","UNIT","FILL UP TO TARGET","Carbs","Recommended for an aggressive cut: 3 meals + snacks. Pre, post and main meal get bigger and more filling, you have fewer eating occasions and stay in the deficit more easily. Use the dinner kcal flexibly as snacks.","Recommended for bulking: 4 meals + snacks. More meals make it easier to hit high kcal without oversized portions.","Tip: 3 meals + snacks are recommended when cutting, 4 when bulking. Otherwise whatever fits your day.","\u2192 Switch to 3 meals","\u2192 Switch to 4 meals","Goal & mode","Meals","Weight & week","App & display","Data","Off \xb7 kcal go to snacks","Meals per day","4 meals","3 meals","Pre-workout, post-workout, main meal, dinner \u2014 pre + post shown as one block.","Pre-workout, post-workout, main meal \u2014 shown separately. Dinner kcal move into snacks.","Grams","= {g} g","Good for {m}","More meals","Weekly deficit","Weekly deficit \xb7 in theory \u2248 {kg} kg fat","\xd8 eaten / day","\xd8 target / day","\xd8 weight","Scale (start \u2192 end of week)","See the data, adjust, keep going \u2013 you're in the game.","Yesterday","Tomorrow","{n} entries \xb7 tap for calendar","Day","Same day","Previous day","Next day","Date \u2026","Move whole meal ({m})","Moved to {d}","Show","\u2605 Favourites","\u2605 Favourites","No favourites yet. Tap the star \u2606 on a food, recipe or meal.","Mark as favourite","Remove favourite","Details","Create food","Create recipe","Ingredients, nutrition, portions, preparation","Edit recipe","Please enter a name and at least one ingredient.","Recipe name","Photo","Ingredients (weighed raw)","Add ingredient","Result","Finished weight (optional)","Portions","Leave empty = sum of ingredients ({g} g). Weighing after cooking is more accurate.","kcal total","per portion ({g} g)","Macros per portion. The recipe is stored per 100 g \u2013 when tracking there is a \u201c1 portion\u201d button.","Preparation","None","Oven","Pan","Pot","Air fryer","Microwave","Blender","Temperature","Stove level (1\u20139)","Time","Steps","One step per line","Tip (optional)","Device","Tip","Prepare all ingredients together.","1 portion \u2248 {g} g \xb7 {k} kcal \xb7 makes {n} portion(s)","Delete recipe","Recipe saved \u2013 find it under Recipes.","Custom portion","Label (e.g. pack, bar, slice)","Amount","Portion","Long-press a custom portion to delete it.","Barcode linked to \u201c{n}\u201d \u2013 recognised directly next time.","Hold the barcode inside the frame","Photo / type","No camera access \u2013 use \u201cPhoto / type\u201d below or allow the camera in settings.","Fill the day","Just keep tracking. The app fills the started meal first, the rest goes to the next one.","Split: {list}","Today","eaten","target range kcal","Volume","Last 7 days","\xd8 eaten / day","\xd8 deficit / day","\xd8 weight","Change this week","In theory: {k} kcal deficit in 7 days \u2248 {dir}{kg} kg (7000 kcal \u2248 1 kg). The scale swings with water \u2013 look at the weekly trend.","Add to shopping list","Raw","Cooked","How many % of your daily target go into this meal. Target = gold mark on the bar, From\u2013To = allowed range.","still free: {p} %","From","To","Target","MEAL TARGET","{m}: check From \u2264 Target \u2264 To (0\u2013100 %).","Fewest kcal per g C/P/F (diet)","Total","Items ({n})","fill to target","Rest day \xb7 carbs \xbd","Rest day (halve pre/post carbs)","Rest day: pre & post-workout carbs halved (\u2212{g} g carbs today).","Rest day off \u2014 normal targets.","Rest day isn't possible on a cheat day.","Category","Taste","tap to open","per 100 g","per portion","Sort","Frequent","A\u2013Z","Fewest kcal first","Most kcal first","Most C/P/F (bulk)","Fiber","Foods","Meals","Recipes","Fill the rest of the day \xb7 into \u201c{m}\u201d","Add meal","Split pre-workout carbs","Complex","Simple","Daily range: {a}\u2013{b} kcal","Pre-workout: complex & simple carbs","Share of your daily carb target. Tap to change.","from","to","Reset (15\u201320 % / 10\u201315 %)","Max possible: {p} % = {g} g (rest of 100 %)","Enter weekly average (instead of daily)","Enter weekly average","If you calculate your average elsewhere. It applies to this week and is used instead of daily values.","Log with photo / time","WEIGHT TODAY","Average last 7 days (kg)","vs. previous week (kg)","Weight saved.","Your trend appears here from 2 entries.","ADJUSTMENT","Smart (weekly)","Fixed (start to end)","Once a week it recalculates with your weekly average weight: progress, days left and \u2014 with a target date \u2014 the kcal per day needed.","Runs once: counts the kcal you actually saved on tracked days.","Realistic muscle share: approx. {a}\u2013{b} kg (depending on training experience), the rest mostly fat & water.","Target weight","Now {w} kg \u2192 {d} kg","PACE","Moderate \xb7 300","Normal \xb7 500","Aggressive \xb7 800","My plan \xb7 {kcal}","Pick target date","Target date: {d}","No date (enter kcal/day)","{dir}{kg} kg \u2248 {total} kcal\nat {kcal} kcal/day \u2192 approx. {days} days\nGoal reached approx. {date}","More than 1000 kcal deficit per day is very hard \u2014 risk of muscle loss.","More than 500 kcal surplus per day mostly adds fat.","Set goal","Small","Medium","Large","Grams = without peel. With peel small / medium / large weigh approx. {s} g.","Grams = with peel. Without peel small / medium / large are approx. {s} g.","Meal (template)","Meals","Ready-made combos. SOL calculates amounts so protein, carbs and fat of this meal fit as closely as possible. Recipes always count as 1 portion.","MY MEALS","SOL MEALS","No meals of your own yet.","New meal","Edit meal","Name (e.g. breakfast shake)","Add food / recipe","Recipe \xb7 1 portion (fixed)","Amounts calculated for this meal. \ud83d\udd12 = recipe, fixed. You can still adjust amounts.","RESULT / TARGET OF THIS MEAL","With plan","Range: {r}","Details","Less","then {kcal} kcal left","then {kcal} kcal over","Open intro & guide","Back up & move data","Saves all PREPIT data (tracking, weight, database, settings) to one file, e.g. to move it into SOL-GYM.","Back up data (file)","Export macro plan (for SOL Planner)","Export failed.","Load data (file)","Load data?","The data from the file replaces the data in this app. PREPIT restarts afterwards.","Choose file","Backup failed.","left after plan: {kcal}","{kcal} over after plan","Search food \u2026","Nothing found.","Eaten","Left","Over","Goal","Display","Overview as ring","Eaten \xb7 Left \xb7 Goal with ring and macro bars. Off = classic bar view.","Photo scan","No barcode found. Get close, hold straight, good light \u2014 try again or type the code.","Type code","Not found \u2014 just enter the food yourself.","Tap \u201cPhoto scan\u201d and take a close, straight photo of the barcode.\n\nToo dark? In the camera tap \u26a1 (top left) \u2192 \u201cOn\u201d to use the flash.","Scanner could not be loaded (internet?). Please type the code.","Type barcode","Digits under the barcode","Search","Help texts","Show help texts","Tips and explanations in tracking (e.g. complex/simple carbs, target notes). Off = cleaner.","Planned \u2014 tick it off once you've eaten it.","PLANNED \xb7 +{kcal} kcal","Eaten \u2713","Remove","Planned, not counted yet. Adjust the amount and confirm as eaten.","Amount","If you eat everything: {kcal} kcal","planned {kcal} kcal","Set goal","Phase goal","Lose","Gain","How much?","Deficit per day","Surplus per day","Your current plan: approx. {kcal} kcal/day","{kg} kg \u2248 {total} kcal\nat {kcal} kcal/day \u2192 approx. {days} days\nGoal approx. {date}","Rough math: 7000 kcal \u2248 1 kg. The countdown adapts: it counts what you actually saved on tracked days.","{n} days to goal","Goal reached \ud83c\udf89","approx.","day","Remove","Consecutive days with at least one log, counting back from today. Nothing logged today = 0.","Day, streak, weight \u2026","Day \u2014 details","Weekly charts and balances: Settings \u2192 Weekly balances.","Avg kcal/day (recent weeks, older on the left)","Scale change per week in kg (green +, red \u2212; line at 0)","Not enough scale entries in these weeks \u2014 no weekly \u0394.","All weeks (list)","Target kcal","Actual kcal","Weight","Weekly balance (calendar week, week start in settings)","Week start (balance & weekly recap)","Monday is common in the EU, Sunday in many US-style apps. Sets which day your week starts (weight delta, recap).","Choose week start","For the weekly balance and recap: which weekday starts your week? (We recommend Monday or Sunday.)","Monday","Sunday","Last week \u2014 recap","A quick look at the completed week up to yesterday. Consistency matters.","Avg intake: {k} kcal/day (7d through week end)","Avg day balance: {d} kcal/day \xb7 sum: {s} kcal (goal \u2212 log, days with a goal)","Avg goal: ~{g} kcal/day (days with a goal)","Scale \u0394 this week: {w} kg (first \u2192 last log)","Avg weight: {w} kg (n={n} entries)","Continue","Good rhythm \u2014 discipline with a deficit is the game. Keep going \u2014 stay on it.","Gaining well takes time. Push training, eat smart, stay consistent.","Read the data, nudge the plan, keep showing up. You\u2019re in the game.","Tap: macros & items","Share of day kcal target: {s}","Weekly balances","Charts and table \u2014 calendar weeks; week start as in \u201cWeek start\u201d.","View weekly balances","Pick a day","Background: your week-start day (balance week).","Period: {from} \u2013 {to}","Day kcal band (week avg, \xb12%): {lo} \u2013 {hi} (avg {mid} kcal)","Mon","Tue","Wed","Thu","Fri","Sat","Sun","Protein first: you\u2019re at least 20g short of today\u2019s target and you\u2019re in your last main meal (snacks not counted) \u2014 prioritize protein now.","7-day view (rolling window, ends on the selected day)","Avg. intake (7d rolling):","Avg. daily balance (goal \u2212 log, days with a cap):","7-day sum (goal \u2212 log, same days):","Day kcal band (avg., \xb12%):","{lo} \u2013 {hi} (avg. {mid} kcal)","Avg. weight (logged days in the window, 7d):","Today (log)","Weight","This calendar week","From your week start through this day. Week start: Settings \u2192 Week start.","Change (scale, calendar week)","Last 7 days (rolling)","Interpretation (model)","Fat-mass equivalent from 7-day kcal balance: \u2248 {eq} kg/week (rule of thumb: 7000 kcal \u2248 1 kg fat).","Rough sustainable-loss ceiling (from body-fat reserve): \u2248 {cap} kg/week.","Scale change on the week: {wa} kg","Kcal surplus \u2248 {eq} kg mass eq./week (not all lean tissue or fat).","Practical upper bound: \u2248 {cap} kg/week","Scale change on the week: {wa} kg","7-day sum (goal \u2212 log, days with a cap): {kcal7} kcal","Scale change: {wa} kg","How satisfied are you with this week\u2019s performance?","Very satisfied","It\u2019s fine","Not so much","When the plan is clicking, you can be proud. Keep pushing \u2014 you\u2019re in rare air. Be proud: you are one of the few who show up. Be the person you want to be as a role model, and make it a little truer every day.","Don\u2019t borrow stress. Your body has its own tempo: the scale wobbles, a few days later it can look very different, and in a surplus performance often bounces back after 1\u20132 real recovery days. Trust your body and focus on what you can steer: full gas in training, clean nutrition\u2014stay on the levers you control.","Tough weeks happen. Water, volume, training, recovery, hormones: the scale can mislead for a while, and that\u2019s normal. No panic. Stay consistent and patient\u2014you\u2019re still steering the inputs that actually matter.","Calories","Protein","Carbs","Fat","of which sugar","Details","Add food","Move\u2026","Move to which meal?","Food and grams stay the same \u2014 only the meal label changes.","Target meal","Move","No other meal to move to.","Move or delete","Scan barcode (Open Food Facts)","Generator","AI photo","kcal","Pre-Workout","Post-Workout","before training","after training","Main meal","Dinner","Breakfast","Lunch","Snacks","Meals","Workout","\u2211 {k} kcal \xb7 pre+post","Pre- & post-workout","Tap: pre- and post-workout open separately (items, macros, tracking)","Tap the title to see pre- and post-workout split below.","Tip: 30\u201390 min before training favor complex carbs (about {cx} % of your daily carb target), right before training favor simple (about {si} %).","Carbs \xb7 complex","Carbs \xb7 simple","Aim: earlier (~30\u201390 min)","Aim: right before training","All","Carbs","Protein","Fat","Fiber","Recipes","Fruit","Vegetables","Also under","All","Cut","Bulk","Cut (high volume)","Bulk (low volume)","Food database","SOL suggestions","Tap to show suggestions & how to read the order","Tap for details. Gold = best for your goal (pick Diet or Bulk above), grey = also fine. Values per 100 g.","Protein","Fat","Fiber","Carbs \xb7 complex","Carbs \xb7 simple","Recipes","Full database below; filter by source and category. Barcode: Open Food Facts; quick add: name + optional photo reference.","Your highlight (softer frame)","For your own foods only. Shown depending on type filter: diet, bulk, or general \u2014 subtler than SOL top picks.","None","Diet","Bulk","General","Your rating (1\u20133)","Optional \u2014 how this food works for you. Narrow the list with the filters below.","Performance","Tolerance","\u2014","weak","ok","top","poor","ok","good","Perf.","Tol.","Performance filter","Tolerance filter","My ratings","Filter by rating","Optional \u2014 filters your 1\u20133 ratings from the food card.","Reset filters","Active: {s}","All","only 3","\u2265 2","rated","none","Source","All","My foods","SOL catalog","Flavor (sweet / savory)","All","Sweet","Savory","Not set","Carb source","Choose carb source","Sustained vs. quick energy","\u201cComplex\u201d carbs usually deliver energy more slowly; \u201csimple\u201d carbs are available fast. This works alongside your listed sugar in the macros.","More whole foods, legumes, longer satiety","Faster to absorb (sugar, juice, etc.)","Edit food","Optional: add a recipe","Barcode Scanner","AI meal (photo)","Enter a Gemini API key from Google AI Studio (free tier may be available). Your photo is sent to Google for analysis \u2014 use only if you are OK with that.","Gemini API key","Photo meal (AI estimates foods & grams)","Add an API key in Settings first.","Settings","Choose photo","Camera or gallery \u2014 good light, dish mostly visible.","Gallery","Camera","AI is analyzing the photo\u2026","No matching foods found.","No foods in the database yet.","API error \u2014 check network, key, or quota.","Request timed out \u2014 try again.","Request blocked \u2014 try a different photo.","Review AI suggestion","Add all","No confident match for \u201c{n}\u201d \u2014 please pick a food.","g","Quick: name (optional photo)","Review & save (per 100 g)","Category in SOL","Network or service error \u2014 try again.","Product not in the database yet \u2014 enter the values from the pack once, then scans will find it.","Code too short \u2014 scan full barcode.","Quick add food","VALUES PER 100 G (OPTIONAL)","Name only; macros start at 0/100g \u2014 fill in the card later (or use the barcode). Optional reference photo, no text recognition yet.","Reference photo (camera)","Photo in cache \u2014 please enter values in the food card later.","Photo (optional)","Gallery","Camera","Remove photo","Complex","Simple","Filter","Search food...","Shopping lists","Share list","List copied \u2014 paste it into any chat.","Today","Monthly","General","Group / store","New group","e.g. grocery chain name","Add note","Free text","From database","Quantity / unit","e.g. 2, 500 g, 1 pack","Add to list","Add all ingredients","Recipe: add ingredients","Remove checked","Nothing on this list yet.","Shopping lists","Add to cart","Move to group","Delete item","Cancel","{n} ingredients","Mode","Delete","Values per 100g","Save","Name","Carbs (total)","of which fiber","of which complex","macros %","Center % = your share of the daily target. Min/max = allowed band. Bars do not use leftover kcal.","Min (%)","Max (%)","Invalid: use 0\u2013100 and min \u2264 max for each macro.","of daily target","One line: e.g. 20, 5\u201312 %, 40 g, 10\u201320 g. Without a range: use buffer (Advanced, below).","%, g, from\u2013to","Buffer (\xb1) per macro (this meal)","For a single % per macro: min\u2013max = center \xb1 buffer. Three sliders \u2014 left = tight, right = loose. If you type an explicit min\u2013max, that wins; buffers apply only to single-number rows.","\xb1 percentage points \xb7 protein","\xb1 percentage points \xb7 carbs","\xb1 percentage points \xb7 fat","This meal (kcal from % min/max): {lo} \u2013 {hi} kcal","Live: {lo}\u2013{hi} %  \u2192  {g1}\u2013{g2} g (day share)","Range from the text field \u2013 buffer slider has no effect here.","Could not read input. Use a number, %, g, or a from\u2013to range (e.g. 5\u201310 or 5\u201310 %).","free","Adjust distribution","The macro distribution is fixed in this mode. Switch to Advanced to set it yourself.","\xb7 of day","Macro distribution","The % in the bar = share of your daily g for this view. The % you enter in the dialog = your target per meal (100% per macro in total).","Day shares: protein (per meal)","Day shares: carbs (per meal)","Day shares: fat (per meal)","Center & min\u2013max per meal","Free: {f}% = {g} g","Total: {s}% (of 100%)","Still available: {r}% = {g} g","Exceeds 100% by {o}%.","Slider per meal \u2014 total max 100%.","Enter a number 0\u2013100 in each field.","Too high: per macro the sum can be 100% max.","Meal Generator","Meal","Missing protein","Missing carbs","Missing fat","Protein source","Carb source","Fat source","Suggestion","Achieved","1 \xb7 Pick protein","2 \xb7 Pick carbs","3 \xb7 Pick fat","4 \xb7 Grams & confirm","\u2014 None (skip this source)","Search\u2026","Back","Quick suggestion (all 3 sources)","The database is missing an item for this mode/category. Try another mode or add manually.","Here are the suggested grams. Adjust if you like, then add to tracking.","You skipped \u201c{m}\u201d while still {g} g short \u2014 you\u2019ll rarely match your goal like this.","This combo is fairly far from your remaining needs (rough total gap ~{s} g across macros).","Amount (g), editable","per 100 g","Scroll the list \u2014 scrollbar on the right","Macro split (this meal)","Percent of daily goal (same as meal settings). \u201cMissing \u2026\u201d below uses this.","Match settings","Save to meal split","SOL recipe ideas","One sweet & one savory pick (top suggestion for your mode).","Use as recipe","No matching recipe in the database.","P","k","F","Note: approximate calculation (combo hard to solve exactly).","Add to tracking","Choose food","Sub-type","SOL suggestion (top pick for your nutrition mode)","Grams","Add","Input","Grams (amount)","Kilocalories (target)","Protein (target, g)","Carbs (target, g)","Fat (target, g)","Value","\u2192 about {g} g","Invalid number, or 0 in per-100g data for that target. Use grams or another target.","Nothing to add: target already met or no room to the band max.","Fill to band","Fill protein","Fill carbs","Fill complex carbs","Fill simple carbs","Fill fat","Fill kcal","Recipe: image, ingredients, steps","Generate (AI) image","No photo yet. Create a matching image with KI (Imagen) \u2013 same API key as in settings (Google AI Studio; Imagen may need to be enabled).","Add your API key in settings.","Could not create image (check quota, API, or Imagen model).","1 serving = {g} g (reference for tracking)","Serving","Grams","Number of servings","Amount (g)","Quick","Target (advanced)","Simple","\u2192 {g} g \xb7 {kcal} kcal \xb7 P {p} \xb7 C {c} \xb7 F {f}","No reference serving set \u2014 use grams or advanced.","SOL calculator","Weight (kg)","Body fat estimate (%)","Estimate body fat","Body fat estimator","What is body fat %?","Body fat percentage (BF%) is the share of your weight that is fat \u2014 the rest is fat-free mass (muscle, organs, water, bone).\n\nSOL uses your BF% to compute your basal metabolism and thus your calorie needs (via fat-free mass). Protein and fat scale directly with bodyweight (2.5 g/kg BW for protein, 0.75 g/kg BW for fat). The more accurate your BF%, the sharper your kcal targets.\n\nReference: men ~10\u201315% = athletic, ~16\u201320% = normal, >22% = visible fat gain. Women physiologically run ~8\u201310 points higher.","Method","Tape (Navy)","Visual match","Sex","Male","Female","Height (cm)","Waist (cm, at navel, relaxed)","Neck (cm, below Adam's apple)","Hip (cm, widest point)","Measure in the morning, relaxed, don't suck in. Accuracy ~\xb13%.","Pick the level closest to your mirror image. Each level has an AI reference illustration. Roughly ~\xb14\u20135%.","Estimated BF%","Reference silhouettes (approx.)","Illustrations are only a rough guide \u2014 real BF% varies with genetics, water, lighting.","Use as BF%","Please fill all fields with plausible values.","Ripped \u2014 deep ab definition, visible vascularity (bodybuilder look)","Athletic \u2014 clear six-pack, strong muscle definition","Fit \u2014 six-pack visible when flexed, flat stomach","Average \u2014 softer stomach, no visible abs","Slight paunch \u2014 softer lines, belly building up","Clear fat gain \u2014 round belly, little muscle definition","Very athletic \u2014 clear muscle definition, visible ab lines","Athletic \u2014 fit, slightly visible abs, defined arms","Fit \u2014 toned, flat stomach, soft definition","Average \u2014 soft contours, no visible abs","Curvier \u2014 more fat at hips/thighs, softer belly","Clear fat gain \u2014 rounder belly and hips","Age","Note: from around 45 the deficit is set more conservatively (muscle protection).","Enter weight, body fat and age, then tap Apply \u2014 required to switch mode.","Cancel","Apply","Got it","Stick to your plan \u2014 focus, discipline!","Understood, I'll stay on track","Heads up!","Your numbers are already at the maximum of what's healthy. Anything you cut beyond that only burns muscle \u2014 not fat.\n\nYour body can break down at most around 70 kcal per kg of body fat per day. Anything more you try on your own goes against nature and against your own discipline.\n\nStick to your plan \u2014 that's how you reach the goal faster than with misplaced ambition.","You've been clearly off your plan for a few days. Eating more doesn't mean growing faster \u2014 the surplus lands as fat, not muscle.\n\nStick to your numbers. Clean growth needs patience and discipline, not blind overshoot.",'"Man does not live by bread alone." \ud83c\udf1e',"Balance","Reset day","Delete all tracking entries?","Clear tracking day","For the day selected in Tracking (calendar) \u2014 same as the old top button.","\xb7 meal center (g)","Weighed at","{k} kg \xb7 {t}","Form update (optional photo)","Gallery","Camera","Saved photo: preview here, under day details (day row), and in day balance.","Reset","Enter weight","Invalid input!","Weight","Open weight dialog in the morning","Between 5:00 and 12:00, the weight dialog appears if you have not logged weight for today (at most once). You can dismiss it without saving \u2014 it will not show again that day.","Maintenance","Aggressive Cut","Lean Bulk","Advanced","Open calculator","Daily goals","Protein goal","Carbs goal","Fat goal","Calories goal","Goal","Stay inside the corridor \u2014 no need to hit a single point, just land between the values.","Amber: soft daily hint (rolling week balance) \u2014 does not change your real day targets or macro bands.","The band readout nudges slightly with your 6-day prior balance (display only).","Balance hint today: {v} kcal","Note: for {n} days in a row, kcal log differs a lot from your daily target \u2014 check rhythm (stress, estimates, or planned breaks).","Ingredients","Instructions","Aggressive Cut: ages 16\u201350 \xb7 Advanced: 16+","Caution \u2014 health risk","Aggressive Cut is only recommended from age 16. While your body is still developing it needs more energy \u2014 not less. Switch to Alltag mode for a balanced setup.","Aggressive Cut is no longer advisable from 50+ \u2014 the risk of muscle loss, hormonal swings and bone density loss is too high. Stay in Alltag mode or pick Lean Bulk to gently maintain.","Advanced assumes a fully developed metabolism \u2014 unlocked from age 16. Use Alltag mode until then for safe, balanced numbers.","Please enter your age in the SOL Calculator first before activating this mode.","Switch to Alltag","Cancel","Gender","Male","Female","Cheatday","Manage cheatday","Cheatday","Today is a cheatday.","Be aware","Be aware of what you\u2019re doing.\n\nA controlled cheatday is okay \u2014 as long as you stay in command of yourself the whole time.\n\nThis mode buys today\u2019s freedom with the progress of the next days. Make the call sober \u2014 never out of impulse.","Activate consciously","Better not","How many days of progress do you sacrifice?","1 day","{n} days","Assumed daily deficit: ~{def} kcal (maintenance \u2212 target). With {n} days sacrificed: +{extra} kcal (today \u2248{total} vs. {base} kcal). Keep the sacrificed days clean afterward.","Crashout (instead of 1\u20134 days)","Crashout: no upper limit, only minimum protein & fat must be covered. Counts as 2 cheatdays. Use it when the brakes have truly snapped \u2014 consciously, not in a frenzy.","Cheatday balance this month","{used} of {max} used","Bonus active (+1) \u2014 you only sacrifice small amounts, that\u2019s rewarded.","Bonus cheatday: if ALL your cheats this month sacrifice \u2264 2 days, you get a 5th one.","No more credits this month. New month starts again at 4.","Today already has a cheatday active.","Remove cheatday again","Cheatday removed for today.","Cheatday activated. Stay in control.","Sacrifice: {n} d \xb7 +{extra} kcal (\u2248{def} kcal/d deficit) \u2192 today \u2248{total} kcal (base {base} kcal)","Crashout \xb7 no upper limit \xb7 minimum protein/fat only","Cheatday active","Eat consciously, enjoy in control \u2014 deliver tomorrow.","Minimum only","no maximum","{used}/{max} credits","Cheatday budget (Advanced)","Default: 4 per month plus 1 bonus if every cheat sacrifices \u22642 days. In Advanced you can set a fixed monthly cap instead.","SOL rule (4+bonus)","Custom monthly max","This month: {used} of {max} credits","Custom monthly cap \u2014 no auto-bonus rule.","Calories on cheat day","\u2248{total} kcal target today","+{extra} kcal over your normal daily target ({base} kcal)","\u2248{per_day} kcal per sacrificed progress day \xd7 {n}","No planned daily deficit \u2014 no bonus above your base target ({base} kcal).","Crashout: no fixed daily cap, so no single kcal number.","Today \u2248{total} kcal \xb7 +{extra} kcal (\u2248{per_day} kcal per sacrificed day \xd7 {n})","Keep the sacrificed days after on plan.","Cheatday on \u2014 today \u2248{total} kcal target (\u2248{per_day} kcal \xd7 {n} sacrificed days).","Edit goals (Advanced)","Auto mode: goals driven by formula","Formula info","Current masses","Maintenance","Macro formulas","\u2022 Protein = 2.5 g \xd7 body weight","\u2022 Fat: Alltag 0.9 g \xb7 Lean Bulk 1.0 g \xb7 Cut 0.75 g \xd7 bodyweight","\u2022 Carbs = remaining calories","Calorie logic by mode","\u2022 Maintenance: calories = maintenance","\u2022 Aggressive Cut: deficit = fat mass \xd7 "," kcal (age adjusted)","\u2192 current deficit: ","\u2022 Lean Bulk: clean surplus (approx. +150 to +300 kcal)","Note: at higher age the deficit is set more conservatively to protect muscle.","Daily goals","Note","No note","Edit note","Thoughts, training, how you feel...","Meal note","Only for this meal on this day (e.g. what you eat, plans, how you feel, notes for the slot).","Check = done, text is struck through. Add lines to remember e.g. electrolytes. \u201eAdd line\u201c for more items.","Add line","e.g. + electrolytes, extra scoop\u2026","Remove line","Show or hide macro table","Tracked foods & amounts","Add food, generator, or AI photo","Tracked: {m}","Nothing here yet. + for food, generator, or AI photo.","g","kcal","Scroll unit and amount, or tap the value \u2014 macros update live.","Enter amount","P","C","F","g only (no usable per-100g kcal or macros).","Arrow: macros. Title: entries. + : food, generator, or AI photo.","Distribution","Performance","Relaxed","Performance = stricter meal split, slightly fewer kcal. Relaxed = more even, slightly more kcal. Also: looser per-meal % bands (widest for fat), slightly wider daily kcal band, fat target ~0.9 g/kg (minimum 0.6 g/kg).","kcal adjustment","Apply","Distribution & kcal updated.","Meal order","Long-press the drag handle and reorder the meals through the day. Pre + Post stay together as one block.","In Alltag & Advanced: every meal is its own row \u2014 Pre- and Post-Workout can be split and moved anywhere. Pencil: rename (only in these modes).","Pre/Post split \xb7 free ordering","Rename meal","Meal name","Name in tracking","Pre + Post \u2014 locked block","Snacks always stay on top and can\u2019t be reordered.","Commitment \u2014 full send","This mode runs at the high end of what\u2019s sane and healthy. It\u2019s not comfortable \u2014 and you\u2019re choosing it on purpose. You follow the plan when it\u2019s hard, because that\u2019s the point.","\u201cDiscipline means going after what\u2019s uncomfortable \u2014 as if it were the dearest thing in the world to you.\u201d","I accept the trade\u2011offs and I stay focused, even when it\u2019s uncomfortable.","I commit","Not now","HERE WE GO \u2014 intensity phase","Aggressive cut / lean bulk: not a comfort cruise. Full consequence, full focus.","Activity level","Independent of extra steps. Sets your maintenance kcal in every mode \u2014 protein and fat stay fixed, carbs adjust.","Very active","Normal","Low everyday","\u2022 Activity ({label}): factor \xd7{factor} on BMR","Movement & cardio (aggressive cut)","Deficit and carbs match your day: extra cardio needs fuel \u2014 very low movement allows a tighter deficit. Extra steps (3,000\u201310,000) add kcal, mostly as carbs.","I want","More cardio","Standard","Less movement","More cardio: slightly milder deficit. Less movement: slightly stronger deficit (for truly low-activity days). Standard: classic SOL math.","Extra steps (your default for targets)","Baseline for kcal (e.g. you move a lot). On an aggressive cut the step add-on stays small (cap ~150 kcal, usually ~100\u2013150 \u2014 not a big food bonus).","Extra steps","\u2248 +{k} kcal from steps (at your weight) with {steps} extra steps.","Extra steps \u2014 this day","Today: custom value (overrides default).","Today: using settings default.","From steps: ~+{k} kcal carbs \xb7 {steps} extra steps","Reset to settings default","Preset","Aggressive Cut","Maintenance","Dirty Bulk","Pick a direction: the further out, the closer to the healthy limit. You can still tweak macros manually.","Apply preset","Man shall not live by bread alone.","Deutsch","English","On-screen help","Daily card (top): tap opens day, streak, weight, and more.\n\nMacro bands: the bars are your actual intake in range. The old italic note about how adjustment and the day balance work is here.\n\nSoft daily kcal nudge: only after 3+ logged days in a row, so a couple of off days don\u2019t swing it.\n\nMeal kcal \u2014 simple: one bar (actual kcal), two marks (lower/upper), target line above, extra room on the right for red. \u2014 advanced: bar = kcal, vertical = lower band edge, green in range.\n\nTap a meal row: macros & line items. Workout: tap to split pre/post; title row, chevron, + menu (food, generator, photo) as when expanded.\n\n7-day block in the day sheet: rolling window ending on the selected day.\n\nDatabase: tap \u201cHighlights\u201d to expand or collapse.\n\nGenerator: long food lists show the scrollbar on the right.\n\nOutside cut mode, pre-workout\u2019s protein % band is intentionally low (about 5\u201314% of that meal\u2019s kcal) \u2014 the 15\u201320% range is a better fit for post (and some cut slots), not a pre focus."],t.li)
